    "rationale": "The objective is the wall latency of one complete GraphEncoder forward (infer.py:53-58 sync-bracketed timing; original baseline 0.36707 ms on the immutable reference revision). Discovery on the current revision shows the whole forward is one contiguous region on the 'model' boundary: call 80ff8693 (group 1f40997fb4a53f41b9da) containing both MeanSAGE layers, both Linear projections and 15 CUDA kernels on a single stream. Measured decomposition (torch-profiler diagnostics, corroborated by the separately collected nsys run, resources.json): GPU kernel busy ~322.8 us of the 367 us clean wall, i.e. ~44 us (~12%) host-dispatch/launch slack even unprofiled, while the nsys-captured span (1291.6 us, 25% busy fraction) is only a perturbed upper bound on gaps. Within the 322.8 us busy time the scatter-based neighbor aggregation chain dominates: aten::index_add_ atomic scatter 145.2 us (99.0 us in layer 2, 46.1 us in layer 1; indexFuncLargeIndex/ReduceAdd, ~0.7 TB/s effective, ~16 duplicate destinations per node), the message-materializing index_select gathers 89.0 us, zeros_like 4.8 us, clamp_min 2.5 us, div 6.9 us, plus cat copies 12.2 us feeding the projections - together ~248 us (77%) of kernel time, and the layer-2 messages tensor (67 MB) also drives the 97 MB peak allocation. These costs are jointly determined by one algorithmic choice spanning both layers (the clamp_min and unsqueeze groups each contain one call per layer, so a single-layer boundary would split shared groups), and the dispatch slack and cat copy span the whole forward. A single-group or per-layer edit therefore cannot address the dominant cost; the coherent editable boundary is the entire encoder forward, replaced as one whole bundle at the module boundary (no inherited bundles are installed: search.json installed_bundles [], resources.json bundles [], so no inherited required calls constrain composition). Excluded: group 3c57c8731ec33ed76cbb / call 5d7d6bb13691b02f533f62b0 (project.in